DexSwapModule_OracleSlippage
├── given oracle is not configured (feeds are zero addresses)
│   ├── when execute is called with low minAmountOut
│   │   └── it should skip oracle check and execute normally
│   ├── when validate is called
│   │   └── it should skip oracle check and return valid
│   └── when estimateOutput is called
│       └── it should return zero estimate with correct target token
├── given oracle is partially configured (only one feed set)
│   ├── when execute is called
│   │   └── it should skip oracle check and execute normally
│   └── when maxSlippageBps is zero but feeds are set
│       └── it should skip oracle check and execute normally
├── given oracle is fully configured
│   ├── when sell token price feed returns negative answer
│   │   ├── it should return failed result in execute with oracle price unavailable
│   │   └── it should return false in validate with oracle price unavailable
│   ├── when buy token price feed returns negative answer
│   │   ├── it should return failed result in execute with oracle price unavailable
│   │   └── it should return false in validate with oracle price unavailable
│   ├── when sell token price feed returns zero answer
│   │   ├── it should return failed result in execute with oracle price unavailable
│   │   └── it should return false in validate with oracle price unavailable
│   ├── when sell token price feed is stale
│   │   ├── it should return failed result in execute with oracle price unavailable
│   │   └── it should return false in validate with oracle price unavailable
│   ├── when buy token price feed is stale
│   │   ├── it should return failed result in execute with oracle price unavailable
│   │   └── it should return false in validate with oracle price unavailable
│   ├── when sell token price feed reverts
│   │   ├── it should return failed result in execute with oracle price unavailable
│   │   └── it should return false in validate with oracle price unavailable
│   ├── when buy token price feed reverts
│   │   ├── it should return failed result in execute with oracle price unavailable
│   │   └── it should return false in validate with oracle price unavailable
│   ├── when decimals() call reverts on a feed
│   │   ├── it should return failed result in execute with oracle price unavailable
│   │   └── it should return false in validate with oracle price unavailable
│   ├── when maxSlippageBps exceeds 10000
│   │   ├── it should return failed result in execute with oracle price unavailable
│   │   └── it should return false in validate with oracle price unavailable
│   ├── when minAmountOut is below oracle floor
│   │   ├── it should revert in execute with SlippageExceedsOracleFloor
│   │   └── it should return false in validate with slippage below oracle floor
│   ├── when minAmountOut equals oracle floor exactly
│   │   └── it should succeed in execute
│   ├── when minAmountOut is above oracle floor
│   │   └── it should succeed in execute
│   ├── when sell and buy tokens have different decimals
│   │   └── it should correctly normalize output across 6 and 18 decimal tokens
│   ├── when price feeds have different decimals
│   │   └── it should correctly normalize using feed decimals
│   └── when estimateOutput is called with oracle configured
│       ├── it should return non-zero expected output
│       └── it should return correct target token
├── validate vs execute ordering — intentional divergence
│   └── when both oracle and balance are invalid
│       ├── validate should report oracle error first (oracle before balance)
│       └── execute should report balance error first (balance before oracle)
└── fuzz
    ├── it should never revert on arbitrary oracle prices and slippage values
    └── it should enforce floor equals expected times (10000 minus maxSlippageBps) over 10000
